summary:
  The settings merge reads an empty field and a missing one as different,
  so it takes the difference for a change made on the page.

history:
  A starred row is saved with prev empty and the page drops an empty prev:
  the heal's prev was taken for a change made here and lost.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ReorderLogic.js

find:
          var v = _blank(c[k]) === _blank(b[k]) ? x[k] : c[k]

replace:
          var v = c[k] === b[k] ? x[k] : c[k]

expect:
  Killed by tst_reorderlogic::test_merge_reads_an_empty_field_and_a_missing_one_alike.
  Line-neutral.
